      "role": "user",
      "content": "I've been reading about DRAGON, OTTER and GIRAFFE and they all sound powerful. Our lab has bulk transcriptomics, proteomics and some ATAC-seq peaks for a mouse model of pulmonary fibrosis, roughly 30 animals across three time points. Which of these should we apply, and what would we actually learn from each? We haven't settled on a specific hypothesis yet, and our PI wants something to show at the next lab meeting."
